---
title: Markdoc
description: Markdoc tags for callouts, tabs, steps, cards, badges and live API operations.
---

[Markdoc](https://markdoc.dev) is Markdown with tags. Name the file `.markdoc`. Headings, the table of contents and code blocks work as in Markdown, and these tags add components. Each example below shows the source, then the result.

## Callout

```markdoc
{% callout type="tip" title="Good to know" %}
Sandbox keys start with `sk_test_`.
{% /callout %}
```

{% callout type="tip" title="Good to know" %}
Sandbox keys start with `sk_test_`.
{% /callout %}

`type` is one of `note`, `info`, `tip`, `success`, `caution`, `warning`, `danger`, `sparkles`, `rocket`, `settings`, `zap`, `lock`, `megaphone`. `icon` picks any other [Phosphor](https://phosphoricons.com) icon. See [Callouts](/docs/writing/callouts/).

## Tabs

````markdoc
{% tabs %}
{% tab name="npm" %}
```bash
npm install @acme/sdk
```
{% /tab %}
{% tab name="pnpm" %}
```bash
pnpm add @acme/sdk
```
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}
````

{% tabs %}
{% tab name="npm" %}
```bash
npm install @acme/sdk
```
{% /tab %}
{% tab name="pnpm" %}
```bash
pnpm add @acme/sdk
```
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

## Steps

```markdoc
{% steps %}
{% step title="Get a key" %}
Create an API key in the dashboard.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Call the API" %}
Send it in the `Authorization` header.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}
```

{% steps %}
{% step title="Get a key" %}
Create an API key in the dashboard.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Call the API" %}
Send it in the `Authorization` header.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

## Cards

```markdoc
{% card-grid columns=2 %}
{% card title="Quickstart" icon="rocket" href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart" %}
A portal in five minutes.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Example API" icon="code" href="/apis/bookstore" %}
See a reference page.
{% /card %}
{% /card-grid %}
```

{% card-grid columns=2 %}
{% card title="Quickstart" icon="rocket" href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart" %}
A portal in five minutes.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Example API" icon="code" href="/apis/bookstore" %}
See a reference page.
{% /card %}
{% /card-grid %}

`columns` defaults to 3. `href` makes the whole card a link; `icon` is a Phosphor icon name.

## Badge

```markdoc
Webhooks {% badge text="Beta" variant="caution" /%}
```

Webhooks {% badge text="Beta" variant="caution" /%}

## API operation

```markdoc
{% api-operation spec="bookstore" path="/books/{bookId}" method="get" /%}
```

{% api-operation spec="bookstore" path="/books/{bookId}" method="get" /%}

Embeds one live operation from an API in `apis:`. See [Embedding operations](/docs/writing/embedding-operations/).

## Workflow

```markdoc
{% workflow file="bookstore" id="findBook" title="Find a book" /%}
```

{% workflow file="bookstore" id="findBook" title="Find a book" /%}

Draws one workflow of a file in [`workflows:`](/docs/configuration/workflows/): `file` is the entry's id, `id` the `workflowId` in the file (default: its first workflow), `view` is `expanded` (the default) or `compact`, and `title` a caption. The tag shows the workflow runner: the diagram with a panel for the inputs and credentials, and **Run workflow** executes the steps from the browser. The same diagram is also generated at build time, so it shows while the runner loads and without JavaScript.

## More tags

| Tag | Does |
| :--- | :--- |
| `aside` | The same as `callout`. |
| `linkcard` | A card that links to a page: `title`, `href` and an optional `description`. |
| `linkbutton` | A link drawn as a button: `href`, and `variant` (`primary`, `secondary`, `minimal`). |
| `filetree` | A folder tree, drawn from the nested list inside it. |

## Showing tag source in a code block

A code fence shows its content as text, tags included, so the examples on this page are plain fences. Markdoc still checks the tags inside a fence, though: an unknown tag or attribute fails the build even inside a code block.

To show tags that aren't valid here, such as a tag from another site or a made-up example, turn the check off with Markdoc's `process=false` annotation after the language:

````markdoc {% process=false %}
```markdoc {% process=false %}
{% my-own-tag color="teal" %}Shown as text, never checked.{% /my-own-tag %}
```
````

Code fences in `markdoc` are highlighted as Markdown.
